Text:  
For IBI MGA, a national leader in insurance brokerage, specializing in the provision of surety bonds in the Construction segment, ABC company Italia Spa is looking for a:

INSURANCE CONSULTANT/SALES ACCOUNT

The professional profile sought is a professional with a commercial background who will have the responsibility to develop a client portfolio starting from certified contact lists and to identify prospect clients, in a stimulating, modern, and highly educational environment.

Requirements:
• Preferred Diploma/Degree;
• VAT number or willingness to open one;
• Experience in commercial roles of direct B2B or B2C sales;
• Customer orientation, ability to work towards objectives, flexibility, and dynamism.

Offered:
• Direct collaboration with the company under a VAT number with the subsequent possibility of internal employment;
• Compensation composed of a fixed part + commissions and bonuses upon reaching target objectives;

Area: Region of competence

To apply, send your resume, including authorization for the processing of personal data, to the following email address: roma.retail@ABC company.it

Availability: Full Time

Means of transport: Car,

Text:  
ABC company Italia Spa is searching for a Quality, Safety, and Environment Employee for a leading company in the food packaging sector located near Cuneo.  

Requirements for the role:  
• Degree in a technical/engineering field;  
• General knowledge of workplace safety regulations (D.Lgs. 81/08);  
• Knowledge of ISO 45001, ISO 14001, and ISO 9001 standards;  
• Ability to interact at all organizational levels;  
• Good spoken and written English skills;  
• Proficiency in Excel and general IT systems, as well as specific software for safety and environmental management;  

A proactive and positive attitude and problem-solving skills complete the profile.  

Direct employment with the company is offered.  
The level of employment will be commensurate with the candidate's experience and competence.  
Work location: near Cuneo (CN).  
Work schedule: full-time daily hours.  

Responsibilities:  
The selected candidate will report directly to the Quality Manager and will take on increasing responsibility in performing the following activities:  

- Support in maintaining ISO Quality System certifications, with the related documentation;  
- Management of quality statistics and internal Non-Conformities and production measurement tools;  
- Management and supervision of workplace safety activities;  
- Monitoring the safety status and compliance with plant rules;  
- Management of internal audits, non-conformities, and corrective actions;  
- Support to the RSPP in developing preventive and protective measures;  
- Management of environmental protection and waste operational and documentary compliance;  
- Support in gathering necessary data for drafting the Sustainability Report;  

Work availability: Full Time  

CCNL: Rubber and Plastics  

Contract level: commensurate with experience

Text:  
ABC company Consultant is seeking, for a leading company in the automotive sector, a position of  

Car Movement Operator  

The role will involve managing all activities related to the movement of cars at the repair workshop site and their proper tracking.  

What you will do:  
• Coordination of the weekly arrivals of cars via car transporters;  
• Collaboration with the team responsible for washing and sanitizing the vehicles;  
• Filing of vehicle documents, back office activities;  
• Movement of cars arriving and departing from the workshop.  

What we require:  
• Proficiency in using main computer tools, especially Excel;  
• Driving license B (essential requirement);  
• Flexibility, reliability, and precision.  

What we offer:  
• Initial fixed-term contract aimed at stabilization within the company;  
• Full Contract 10  
• Concrete opportunities for professional growth in a highly meritocratic and international environment.  

Working hours availability: Full Time

