Text:  
ABC company Consultant Technical & Engineering is seeking, for a leading company in the automotive sector, a position of  

Auto Mechanic  

The resource will be responsible for the mechanical evaluation of used vehicles and their restoration for direct sale to private customers.  

Main duties:  
• Evaluation of necessary restorations for vehicle resale;  
• Independently perform mechanical work commissioned by the team leader;  
• Carry out electronic work and electronic diagnostics;  
• Perform servicing, brake replacement, pads;  
• Replace and repair tires;  
• Check the quality of the work performed.  

Required skills:  
• Middle school diploma and/or high school diploma;  
• Previous experience, at least two years, in the Automotive sector and mechanical repair in a workshop;  
• Good manual skills in using work tools;  
• Ability to work in a team;  
• Good use of specific programs and diagnostic software.  

What we offer:  
• Contract and classification commensurate with the actual experience gained in the role;  
• Energetic, young, and informal environment;  
• Training courses and participation in industry fairs and events;  
• Concrete opportunities for professional growth in a highly meritocratic and internationally expanding context.  

RAL: up to 27K  
Work location: Teodora (PV)  
Working hours: Full Time, 40 hours.  

Availability: Full Time

Text:  
ABC company branch in Melegnano is searching for a leading company in the metalworking sector, the position of:  

MAINTENANCE TECHNICIAN  

The ideal candidate will be responsible for:  
- planning, managing, and implementing internal and external maintenance of all company production assets according to TPM (total productive maintenance), or in case of failure, both mechanically and electrically;  
- managing collaboration with suppliers;  
- managing and ordering spare parts for company production assets;  
- providing reports on preventive and extraordinary maintenance costs;  
- supporting the Industrialization office in the development of new equipment aimed at improving productivity, ergonomics, and operator safety;  
- managing the entire process through our Cloud system, to keep track of historical maintenance data of all machinery/equipment.  

Required qualifications:  
- diploma in mechanical/electrical field;  
- at least 5 years of experience in the role;  
- ability to read and interpret technical specifications from brochures, drawings, and electrical diagrams;  
- knowledge of Microsoft Office;  
- in-depth knowledge of production processes (preferably on CNC machines and/or assembly);  
- preferable knowledge of the English language (minimum level A2);  
- organizational and team collaboration skills;  
- preferable PES PAV certification.  

Offered:  
- Direct employment in the company with a permanent contract;  
- Salary commensurate with seniority;  
- Metalworking National Collective Labor Agreement + meal vouchers;  
Workplace: Melegnano (MI).  

Work experiences:  
Maintenance mechanic (machines) (m/f) - 120 months  

Education:  
Qualification / Certificate  

Availability: Full Time  

Driver's license: B  

Means of transport: Car,

Text:  
ABC company Italia Spa is looking for an insurance agent for a company in Legnano.  
The selected candidate, with previous experience in the role and mandatory RUI registration, will be responsible for:  
- updating their collaborators;  
- planning and organizing the agency's activities;  
- providing insurance advice to their clients;  
- managing the economic-administrative relationships between their agency, the insured, and the company;  
- drafting policies and premiums.  

RUI registration and good knowledge of the sector are required.  
Working hours: 37.5 hours per week from Monday to Friday, from 9 AM to 12:30 PM and from 2:30 PM to 6 PM.  
An initial temporary contract is offered, with the possibility of permanent employment.  

Availability: Full Time  

Driver's License: B

Text:  
For a leading company in the footwear sector, located near Asolo, we are looking for an import office clerk.  

Candidates with previous experience will be primarily considered. However, candidates with basic training who are open to a growth path within the company will also be evaluated.  

An initial fixed-term contract is expected, with the possibility of subsequent confirmation.  

The ideal candidate possesses:  
• 3/4 years of experience in a similar role;  
• Experience in managing sea and air shipments;  
• Knowledge of the market and main logistics operators;  
• Knowledge of customs operations;  
• Good knowledge of MS Office;  
• Good knowledge of the English language;  
• Dynamic personality, proactivity, and practical approach;  
• Analytical and communication skills, problem-solving.  

Responsibilities:  
The ideal candidate:  

• Ensures the customs clearance of shipments, coordinating the flow of information for product importation, collecting necessary documents from suppliers or involved internal parties;  
• Follows the importation of products, verifying and confirming the booking made by buyers to suppliers and coordinating logistics and delivery to company warehouses;  
• Identifies and assigns the correct customs code in the system for product importation, based on final product development information;  
• Reviews and verifies import-related invoices (carriers and customs) to proceed with payment (through the accounts payable department).  

Working hours: Full Time  

Driver's license: B  

Means of transport: Car,

Text:  
ABC company Italia Spa is seeking, for an important company in the area, a Corporate Office Assistant.  
The candidate, with a degree in Law and experience in the legal field, will be responsible for:  

- Preparing documents for the convening of Board of Directors and Shareholders' Meetings, taking minutes, and transcribing sessions;  
- Ensuring the collection of original signatures on Meeting and Assembly Minutes, managing their registration, scanning, and archiving;  
- Guaranteeing the execution of operational activities for the filing and registration of documents in support of the company's tax office;  
- Carrying out operational and support activities as requested by the Supervisory Bodies of the Group's Companies;  
- Requesting opinions from the external Corporate Law Consultant, as required by the Function Manager;  
- Handling the validation of corporate books;  
- Interfacing with Notaries for the preparation of documents related to extraordinary operations, granting of powers, revision of Statutes or Articles of Incorporation;  
- Providing operational support to the Transparency and Anti-Corruption Manager in carrying out activities as required and delegated;  
- Collaborating with the Administration, Finance, and Control Function for the preparation of documentation related to activities involving this Function, including interactions with the Revenue Agency for fulfilling related obligations;  
- Providing operational assistance for general office activities, including entering Purchase Requests related to the Function in the Navision management system.  

Technical-professional skills:  
Legal area, expertise in civil and administrative law, specific to the regulations overseen.  

Working hours: 38 hours per week from Monday to Thursday from 8:00/9:30 AM (flexible start) and leaving after 8 hours, with a 45-minute break between 12:00/2:00 PM. On Fridays, work ends at 2:00 PM.  
Temporary employment, aimed at stable hiring in the company.  

Availability: Full Time  

Driver's License: B

Text:  
ABC company Italia S.p.A. is seeking a Beauty Advisor for SEPHORA, a well-established company in the retail world, specializing in the sale of cosmetics and personal care products.  
The selection is dedicated to individuals with the requirement of protected category, as per law 68/99.  

Role  
As a Beauty Advisor, particularly in the Bologna team, you will excel and enjoy this position if you are ready to manage the following activities:  
• Welcome customers, ensuring they have a unique and memorable shopping experience: make them feel pampered, listened to, and well-advised;  
• Offer personalized consultations based on the type of customer;  
• Support the Store Manager and Specialists in managing daily activities;  
• Actively contribute to achieving the Store's goals (budget and targets), adapting to any strategy changes and new action plans set by your managers;  
• Organize and manage the stockroom and deliveries;  
• Contribute to creating a strong team spirit, collaborating with your team colleagues and fostering a positive atmosphere.  

Requirements  
• Previous experience in similar roles (Sales Assistant, Promoter, Beauty Consultant), preferably in dynamic multinational Retail environments;  
• Knowledge of key retail KPIs;  
• Empathy and dynamism;  
• Results-oriented;  
• Teamwork predisposition.  

Work location: Bologna.  
Work schedule: part-time, with shifts to be defined based on the store.  

Why join the SEPHORA team  
• Working Environment: you will work in a dynamic and inclusive environment and can participate in company events;  
• Work-life balance: organize your workweek over 5 days;  
• Sephora Stands: the 'Sephora Stands' committee organizes activities with a positive social and environmental impact;  
• Career paths: continue to develop your skills through personalized training and development plans created by the “Sephora University”;  
• Meaningful Rewards: access to company welfare, receive beauty products as gifts, and access discounts on Sephora and LVMH products.  

Availability: Part-time morning

Text:  
ABC company is seeking a Test Room Technician for a company operating in the industrial electrical sector, specializing in the design, production, and testing of high voltage electrical equipment (bushing insulators), located in Sesto San Giovanni.  

The candidate will be integrated into the production cycle (high voltage test room) and will be responsible for:  
• Testing and inspection activities of electrical components (high voltage bushing insulators) in accordance with international standards, procedures, and applicable technical/quality/safety operating instructions;  
• Mechanical and electrical setup activities for various test configurations;  
• Use of dedicated electronic equipment and instrumentation with related software;  
• Performing FAT (Final Acceptance Test) in the presence of clients and/or third-party inspectors;  
• Post-processing of data and drafting test reports using dedicated software programs;  
• Collaborating in maintaining the calibration of electronic instrumentation and measurement chains;  
• Collaborating with different production departments (finishing, quality control, packaging, production) to ensure delivery.  

Essential characteristics:  
• High school diploma with a technical focus (electrical, electronic, mechatronic technician);  
• Availability to work in shifts (except Saturday and Sunday);  
• Experience, even brief, in testing, quality control, or production inspections;  
• Ability to interpret test specifications and technical drawings, even in English;  
• Aptitude for testing activities, with a propensity for manual work (simple mechanical tasks, handling test objects and materials using internal handling equipment);  
• Availability for overtime if needed;  
• Good knowledge of the Office package;  
• Reliability, seriousness;  
• Problem-solving skills.  

A permanent contract is offered.  
Availability to work on 3 shifts is required (6:00/14:00- 14:00/22:00- 22:00/6:00).  

Salary: 28K-32K.  
National Collective Labor Agreement for the Chemical Pharmaceutical Industry.  

Work availability: Shift work with night shifts.

Text:  
ABC company Italia Spa is seeking, for a well-established company specializing in the supply of construction equipment based in Calenzano,  

a warehouse worker with technical coordination functions.  

The sought-after candidate will mainly be responsible for:  
• Warehouse management: receiving goods, restocking the warehouse, and unloading the warehouse for spare parts management  
• Supporting the branch technical assistance manager in organizing repair interventions by service technicians;  
• Supporting the technical resources coordinator to ensure maximum flexibility and quality of response to customers;  
• Handling administrative tasks related to technical assistance;  
• Managing tasks related to work orders  

Requirements:  
• Diploma in a technical field, or similar competence;  
• Passion for the relevant sector;  
• Excellent proficiency with main computer systems  
• Forklift operation  

The profile is completed by:  
• Good written and verbal communication skills;  
• Teamwork inclination;  
• Planning and organizational skills.  

The working hours are full-time, Monday to Friday.  

A 6 + 6 month temporary contract is offered, with a strong possibility of contract stabilization at the end of the period.  

Availability: Full Time

Gruppo Lactalis Italia, for the BU Galbani Cheese, is looking for recent graduates in Economics interested in embarking on a professional growth path within the commercial world, Van Selling area. The resources, inserted in a sales attempt context, will have the opportunity to develop technical and managerial skills by operating directly in the field, through dedicated training and shadowing activities.

In the initial phase, the resources will be supported by a territorial manager who will train and assist them in the role of seller, with the aim of increasing, through sales and negotiation techniques, the commercial potential of the assigned area, where Lactalis already has an important sales network.

Responsibilities:
In particular, the activities will be as follows:
• Develop the turnover of the assigned area by exploiting the commercial opportunities provided monthly by the company to capture the market potential;
• Promote the product portfolio consisting of important historical Italian brands (Galbani, Cademartori, Vallelata, Invernizzi, and Locatelli);
• Increase the customer base provided by the company by developing the HO.RE.CA channel and the Traditional Trade channel;
• Deliver products to customers daily through a van provided by the company;
• Manage the commercial and payment conditions of the clients.

Required Requirements
• Degree in economic disciplines or related fields;
• Strong interest in the sales world and willingness to embark on a managerial path within it;
• Availability for geographical mobility across the national territory will be an essential requirement;
• Sales experience in the food sector, preferably in the ho.re.ca channel, will be positively evaluated.
• Driving license B
• Proactivity, determination, initiative, excellent relational and communication skills complete the profile.

An initial 12-month fixed-term contract is expected, followed by further development opportunities based on the potential expressed and the results obtained. For the first year, the company will support the resource in relocation.

Location: ITALY – prerequisite: availability for territorial mobility throughout the national territory.

SELECTION PROCESS: AN ASSESSMENT DAY IS SCHEDULED FOR LATE MARCH/EARLY APRIL 2025
START DATE: APRIL 2025

Work availability: Full Time

Driving license: B

