Text:  
ABC company Italia Spa is seeking an IT technician for a company specializing in industrial plant engineering and automation located near Cuneo.  

The resource, hired with a focus on growth and development, will be responsible for managing and improving the company's information systems, ensuring high standards in terms of performance and security, reporting directly to the group's IT Director.  

Requirements  
• Bachelor's degree in Computer Science or equivalent education  
• At least 2 years of previous experience in similar roles  
• Troubleshooting skills for hardware and software issues  
• Knowledge of Microsoft 365 applications and their functionalities (Outlook, Teams, OneDrive, SharePoint, etc.) and virtualization environments based on VMware Vsphere or similar  
• Networking: knowledge of TCP – UDP protocols, Routing, knowledge of security protocols  
• Skills in configuring and managing Firewalls (preferably Fortinet)  
• Knowledge of IT security principles, backup & replication systems (e.g., Veeam)  
• Good knowledge of English (written and spoken)  
• Availability for short trips to other company locations  

A proactive and positive attitude and problem-solving skills complete the profile.  

Direct employment in the company is offered.  
Level of employment commensurate with experience  

Responsibilities:  
Specifically, the resource will be responsible for carrying out the following activities:  

- Level I and II support to users onsite and through a ticketing system;  
- Management of the company's network and IT infrastructure in coordination with the external IT consulting company and according to the group's directives (Client, Server, Switch, VLAN, VPN, Wifi, etc.);  
- Installation, configuration, and domain integration of devices according to group standards;  
- Management and configuration of Microsoft365 (Teams, SharePoint, OneDrive, etc.);  
- Training users on the group's IT tools;  
- Management, maintenance, and backup of company servers (Windows Server, VMware, VEEAM, etc.);  
- Analysis, selection, management, and configuration of business-dedicated software;  
- Management of IT suppliers and company equipment (PCs, Smartphones, Badges, Documentation): purchasing, configuration, and support;  
- Software installation and application of Group Policies;  
- Management of mobile and fixed telephony, FileServer, and network folders;  
- Configuration of printers, multifunction devices, and other network devices;  

Working hours: Full Time  

CCNL: Metalworking  

Contract level: commensurate with experience

