Text:  
ABC company Italia Spa is searching for a solid and structured company, a leader in the Chemical Sector - Automation in the Valsamoggia (BO) area:  

ELECTRONIC MAINTENANCE TECHNICIAN - EXPERT IN PLC AND AUTOMATION ISSUE RESOLUTION  

The candidate has completed training in Electrical/Electronic Engineering and has at least 2 years of experience in the sector.  

The resource, integrated into the Engineering team, will be responsible for defining and implementing the maintenance strategy for new equipment as well as optimizing the existing strategy with a focus on continuous improvement.  

Requirements:  
- Availability to work on 3 shifts, continuous cycle  
- Previous experience in executing/improving electronic maintenance cycles;  
- Ability to identify electronic faults and perform software, electronic, automation, and digital system debugging on the line;  
- Ability to solve electronic problems on: industrial sensors (optical, inductive, capacitive, laser, temperature), brushless servomotors, asynchronous motors;  
- Advanced knowledge of the following automation systems: Beckhoff Twincat V2 and V3, Siemens Simatic S7, Siemens Simotion Scout;  
- Basic knowledge of the following automation systems: Schneider SoMachine LMC, Elau Epas4;  
- Basic knowledge of the following vision systems: Cognex Insight, Cognex Dataman, Omron FH  

Permanent contract with an interesting and adequate salary based on skills, housing support for non-residents in the area, and other company benefits.  

Responsibilities:  
Specifically, the candidate will:  
- Ensure compliance with safety standards, following company policies and guidelines on environment, health, safety, and sustainability;  
- Promote a safety culture that encourages the use of a preventive/predictive approach in line with Open+/IOS;  
- Develop digital and electrical control strategies to ensure the availability of documentation in critical situations;  
- Contribute to the design phase of digital and automation solutions/products that provide technical information on the current state of the company (data, hardware, software, firmware, etc.);  
- Manage software and hardware changes among different types of equipment;  
- Support the Asset Engineer/Tech Lead during the monitoring and analysis of spare parts consumption, costs, and overheads to align with the company budget;  
- Collaborate in the implementation of any appropriate countermeasures to minimize losses;  
- Define material for internal technical training;  

Work availability: Full Time
